  "/blog/stop-human-approval-in-pull-requests-for-better-collaboration.html": {
    "replies": [
      {
        "name": "Márton Salomváry",
        "profile": "https://mastodon.berlin/@mrc",
        "avatar": "/assets/avatars/e12606692f7002c4.jpg",
        "url": "https://mastodon.berlin/@mrc/111923620058859041",
        "published": "2024-02-13",
        "text": "@yvg Perfect timing, need exactly this on a project I recently joined. \n\nThey practice the classic PR review ceremony. I the past few weeks since I've been collaborating, it has prevented zero bugs and facilitated zero meaningful conversations.\n\nMeanwhile it delayed delivery by a day on the average and created 5-10% time overhead by creating merge conflicts.\n\nGreat write-up, thanks! Will drop this bomb on this team soon :D Long live Trunk Based Development!"
      },
      {
        "name": "Márton Salomváry",
        "profile": "https://mastodon.berlin/@mrc",
        "avatar": "/assets/avatars/e12606692f7002c4.jpg",
        "url": "https://mastodon.berlin/@mrc/111923632930578259",
        "published": "2024-02-13",
        "text": "@yvg Speaking of merge conflicts, that's an important side-effect of PRs you might want to mention in your post. The longer a merge is delayed, the more and bigger the merge conflicts will be.\n\nAnd, partially as a result of the above, collaborators will end up creating bigger PRs, that should have been small, separate, individually shipped changes."
      },
      {
        "name": "Yves Van Goethem",
        "profile": "https://indieweb.social/@yvg",
        "avatar": "/assets/avatars/2c22b564d0d93249.jpg",
        "url": "https://indieweb.social/@yvg/111923633925772685",
        "published": "2024-02-13",
        "text": "@mrc Yep, TBD is a nice goal, short scoped PRs without human approval is already a great improvement ;b\nWhat helps is to track metrics, I wanted to add it to the article but it was difficult to extract meaningful data from a historical db to make public without organisational context and data points, soooo I abandoned."
      },
      {
        "name": "Yves Van Goethem",
        "profile": "https://indieweb.social/@yvg",
        "avatar": "/assets/avatars/2c22b564d0d93249.jpg",
        "url": "https://indieweb.social/@yvg/111923644619766147",
        "published": "2024-02-13",
        "text": "@mrc Agree, for the sake of reading length I mostly focused on one aspect of PRs, there is a lot more to say, be it merges, long lived PRs, CI, costs, etc."
      },
      {
        "name": "Márton Salomváry",
